    POD::Coverage is a bit too strict

    Right, because i don't really like privatizing functions
    just to tell people off about breaking implementation
    details, so I don't really prefix them with underscores...
    (I mean don't get me wrong, I don't like access modifiers
    that reinforce private-ness without obfuscation either, or
    I would be happily writing Java libraries.  It's just that
    having to use underscore to "hide" features from user as
    if it's some hideous monster has always thrown me off...)

    and also because *want is only defined conditionally if we
    cannot import Want.  It's not really our function, so this
    has to be called off.

